# Question: does `ze config validate` refuse an unregistered login-service name
# under system/authorization/login-service/service, naming the bad value,
# stating this build does not offer it, and listing the offered services, while
# accepting registered service names?
# Why a unit test cannot decide it: unit tests exercise LoginServiceValidator in
# isolation; only `ze config validate` proves the YANG ze:validate binding,
# RegisterValidators wiring, validatedSections walk, and every surface's init()
# registration compose in the real binary.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-9 -- unregistered login-service name refused naming offered services
# PREVENTS: LoginServiceValidator registered without reaching system/authorization/login-service/service

stdin=invalid:terminator=EOF_INVALID
system {
	authorization {
		login-service bad-set {
			service [ ssh bogus-door ]
		}
	}
}
EOF_INVALID

stdin=valid:terminator=EOF_VALID
system {
	authorization {
		login-service all-doors {
			service [ ssh web rest grpc mcp ]
		}
	}
}
EOF_VALID

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=invalid
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=login service "bogus-door" is not offered by this build
expect=stdout:contains=offered:
expect=stdout:contains=grpc
expect=stdout:contains=mcp
expect=stdout:contains=rest
expect=stdout:contains=ssh
expect=stdout:contains=web
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=valid
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
